      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(anthropic): don't crash models list when a configured Sonnet 5 model has no cost",
        "body": "## Problem\n\n`openclaw models list` aborts with:\n\n```\nTypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'input')\n    at applyAnthropicSonnet5Cost (register.runtime)\n```\n\nwhenever the user config supplies an Anthropic Sonnet 5 model row without `cost` metadata — e.g. a bare `agents.defaults.models[\"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5\"]` runtime binding. `applyAnthropicSonnet5Cost` compares `params.model.cost.input` unconditionally.\n\n## Fix\n\nOptional chaining on the cost comparison. A costless model falls through the equality check and gets the canonical Sonnet 5 cost applied, which is the intended normalization.\n\n## Test\n\nAdded a regression test: normalizing a Sonnet 5 model with `cost: undefined` no longer throws and returns the canonical cost. Verified it fails on main and passes with the fix.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "branch": "fix/models-list-sonnet5-cost-crash",
